; ---- Backup pages
BackupTitle=Save or restore a backup?
BackupDescription=Carry your drivers, Wi-Fi networks and apps from one Windows to the next.
BackupNone=Don't use a backup
BackupExport=Save a backup of this PC
BackupImport=Restore a backup
BackupBeforeFormat=before formatting
BackupAfterFormat=after formatting
BackupInfo=Before formatting, save the backup to a USB drive or another disk you won't erase. After reinstalling Windows, open this installer again and choose to restore it.
BackupInfoWhat=The backup holds the manufacturers' drivers (graphics, sound, chipset, network...) and, if you want, your Wi-Fi networks with their passwords and the list of your apps. It doesn't hold your files.
ExportTitle=Where should the backup go?
ExportDescription=Choose a USB drive or another disk you won't format.
ExportPrompt=Destination folder:
ExportInfo=If the folder doesn't exist, it will be created. After formatting, open the installer from that same disk: it will suggest this backup.
ExportAppList=Also save the list of installed apps
ExportWifi=Also save the Wi-Fi networks with their passwords (they're readable in the backup)
ImportTitle=Where is the backup?
ImportDescription=Choose the folder you saved before formatting.
ImportPrompt=Backup folder:
ImportFound=There's a backup next to the installer: %1. If it isn't yours, choose another one.
ImportHint=It's the Drivers_PC-NAME folder created by the backup.
ImportWhat=The apps you had are checked on the next page, where you can change them.
ImportDrivers=Restore the drivers
ImportWifi=Restore the Wi-Fi networks
DirMissingTitle=Enter a folder
DirMissingText=Type the path or click Browse.
SameDriveTitle=The folder is on the same drive as Windows (%1)
SameDriveText=If you format that drive, you'll lose the backup. A USB drive or another disk is best.
SameDriveKeep=Save it there anyway
ChooseOtherFolder=Choose another folder
PathTooLongTitle=The folder is too long for the drivers
PathTooLongText=Windows doesn't allow paths longer than 260 characters. With this folder, which already takes %2, some drivers of this PC would need paths of %1. A folder of up to %3 characters works.
UseFolder=Use %1
ImportPathTooLongTitle=The backup is in a folder that is too long
ImportPathTooLongText=Some files of the backup have paths of %1 characters, and Windows doesn't allow more than 260: they couldn't be read. Move the folder somewhere shorter, for example %2, and choose it again.
ExportPathHint=The backup folder is too long (%1 characters): Windows doesn't allow paths longer than 260 and some drivers don't fit. Save the backup again in a shorter folder, such as %2.
DirNotFoundTitle=The folder doesn't exist
EmptyBackupTitle=There's nothing to restore in that folder
EmptyBackupText=I can't find drivers (.inf), Wi-Fi networks or an app list in it or in its subfolders.
ContinueAnyway=Continue anyway

