; ---- Options page
OptionsTitle=Settings and options
OptionsDescription=Choose what else to do before and after installing.
OptionsInfo=The Windows settings come from WinUtil, by Chris Titus Tech (MIT license). The recommended ones are already checked; click any of them to see what it does. To be able to undo everything, check the restore point.
OptionHint=Click a setting to see what it does.
OptGroupSuggestions=Suggestions for this PC
OptFolders=Keep Documents, Downloads, Pictures, Videos and Music on %1
OptFoldersDesc=In %1\<your user name>, off the Windows drive: they take no room there and survive a reformat. If they exist from before, they're used as they are; what the current ones hold isn't moved.
DriveFree=%1 (%2%3 GB free)
OptGroupBefore=Before starting
OptGroupParallel=Installing the apps
OptParallelOne=One at a time
OptParallelMany=%1 at a time
OptParallelRecommended=%1 (recommended for this PC)
OptParallelDesc=Several at a time finish sooner: while one installs, others download. Microsoft Store apps always go one at a time, and if two installers clash, it's retried. This PC: %1.
ParallelWhyPc=%1 logical processors and %2 GB of RAM
ParallelWhyVm=a virtual machine, best one at a time
OptRestorePoint=Create a system restore point
OptRestorePointDesc=If something doesn't convince you, "System Restore" takes Windows back to how it was before starting. If System Protection is off, it asks you before turning it on.
; The Windows tweaks and their groups are in catalog_tweaks.csv
OptGroupAfter=When finished
OptUpgradeAll=Also update all apps already installed (WinGet)
OptUpgradeAllDesc=At the end, WinGet updates everything it knows how to update, including what was already installed.

