CreatingRestorePoint=Creating a restore point...
RestoreCreated=created
RestoreRecent=there was already one from the last 24 hours
RestoreFailed=couldn't be created (%1)
RestoreHint=System protection may be turned off by a policy on this PC.
RestoreTurnedOn=created; System Protection was off and is now on
ProtectionTitle=Turn on System Protection?
ProtectionText=System Protection is off on %1, and without it no restore point can be created.
ProtectionAction=If you turn it on, it will use at most %1 of the drive and stay on. At the end, the log will tell you how to turn it off once you see everything works.
ProtectionYes=Yes, turn it on and create the point
ProtectionNo=No, no restore point
ProtectionLimit=System Protection will use at most %1 of the drive.
ProtectionHowToOff=To turn it off once you see everything works (this deletes the restore points): Disable-ComputerRestore -Drive '%1\' in PowerShell as administrator, or System Protection > Configure > Disable system protection.
ApplyingTweakCount=Setting %1 of %2: %3
TweakApplied=Applied: %1
TweakFailed=Couldn't apply: %1
TweaksRestartNote=Some changes show up after restarting or signing in again.
TweaksApplied=%1 applied
TweaksSomeFailed=%1 of %2 couldn't be applied: %3
TweaksHint=The details are in the settings task.
UpgradingAll=Updating everything installed...
UpgradeDone=everything up to date
UpgradeFailed=some couldn't be updated (%1)
UpgradeHint=Run winget upgrade to see which ones are left.
