FoldersDetail=Documents, Downloads, Pictures, Videos and Music to %1, in a folder with your user name.
MovingFolders=Changing where your folders are...
FoldersMoved=now on %1 (shows after restarting)
FoldersFailed=some couldn't be changed
FoldersHint=The details are in the personal folders task.
FoldersUndo=To put a folder back: its Properties > Location > Restore Default.

; ---- WinGet
NoWingetTitle=WinGet isn't available on this PC
NoWingetText=Open Microsoft Store, update "App Installer" and run this installer again.
NoInternetTitle=No Internet connection
NoInternetText=All apps are downloaded from the Internet, so none can be installed without a connection.
NoInternetAction=Connect (for example, to Wi-Fi) and click Retry.
NoInternetReason=no Internet connection
Retry=Retry
CancelInstall=Cancel the installation
; Language passed to the Battle.net installer (--lang)
BlizzardLanguage=enUS
WgInstalled=installed
WgInstalledReboot=installed; a restart is needed
WgUpToDate=up to date
WgOtherVersion=with another version (left as it was)
WgCantUpgrade=WinGet can't update it (left as it was)
WgWasOpen=not updated because it was open
WgWasOpenHint=Close it and update it with winget upgrade if you want the latest version.
WgBusy=another installation was in progress (Windows Update?)
WgBusyHint=Try again when it finishes.
WgRebootFirst=a restart is needed before installing it
WgRebootFirstHint=Restart and try again.
WgNoElevation=its installer doesn't support administrator
WgNoElevationHint=Open this installer by double-clicking it, not with "Run as administrator".
WgUnknownId=its ID doesn't exist in WinGet
WgUnknownIdHint=Check the ID in catalog_apps.csv (winget search <name>).
WgNotApplicable=not compatible with this PC
WgDownload=the download failed or there's no connection
WgDownloadHint=Check the Internet connection and try again.
WgHash=the downloaded installer isn't the expected one
WgHashHint=It usually fixes itself when WinGet updates the package; try again later.
WgDiskFull=out of disk space
WgDependency=a dependency is missing or couldn't be installed
WgCancelled=the installer was cancelled
WgPolicy=blocked by a policy on this PC
WgInstallerFailed=its installer failed (%1)
WgInstallerCode=its installer failed (it ended with code %1)
WgErrorHint=More information: winget error 0x%1
WgNoNvidia=This PC has no NVIDIA graphics card, and its installer only runs with one.
WgStoreCertificate=Microsoft Store failed its certificate check
WgStoreCertificateHint=It usually comes from an old App Installer (common right after formatting) or from an antivirus, proxy or VPN that inspects HTTPS connections. Update "App Installer" from the Microsoft Store and install them again; if nothing changes, turn off that inspection or the VPN. Last resort, in an administrator console: winget settings --enable BypassCertificatePinningForMicrosoftStore
WgSourceNotReady=WinGet couldn't open its sources
WgNotReadyHint=It usually happens right after formatting, while Windows updates App Installer. Try again in a few minutes.
UpdatingAppInstaller=Microsoft Store's certificate doesn't match: App Installer (WinGet) is updated once and the app is retried.
StorePinningTitle=Microsoft Store fails WinGet's certificate check
StorePinningText=WinGet requires Microsoft Store to use one of its known certificates and gets a different one here, even after trying to update App Installer. It's usually an antivirus, proxy or VPN that inspects HTTPS connections.
StorePinningAction=I can make WinGet check the Store the way Windows does (the connection stays encrypted and verified) only during this installation. When it finishes, WinGet's own check is turned back on.
StorePinningYes=Yes, only during the installation
StorePinningNo=No, leave those apps out
StorePinningOffDetail=Until the installation ends, WinGet checks Microsoft Store the way Windows does (BypassCertificatePinningForMicrosoftStore).
WgNotLaunched=couldn't run WinGet
WgSkipHint=Its installer may have been waiting for an answer. Install it manually whenever you like; if it was left half-done, reinstall it.
WgCutHint=It was cut short by Cancel: if it was left half-done, reinstall it.

; ---- End and restart
StatusCancelled=Cancelled.
StatusWarnings=Finished; some tasks need review.
StatusOk=Finished successfully.
FinishedTitle=Finished
FinishedDescription=The log has opened and stays on your Desktop. Click Next to finish.
FinalCounts=Installed now: %1   Already there: %2   Not installed: %3
NotProcessed=not processed
NotProcessedWhy=not processed (%1)
RestartNeededTitle=A restart is needed to finish. Restart now?
RestartQuestion=Do you want to restart the PC now?
RestartNow=Restart now
RestartLater=Later
; Restarting towards the Windows installer USB after saving a backup
UsbRestartTitle=Restart to install Windows?
UsbModeUefi=UEFI boot: the PC can restart straight into the boot menu.
UsbModeBios=Classic BIOS boot (Legacy): the USB is chosen while the PC starts.
UsbSecureBoot=Secure Boot is on: the USB must be an official one.
UsbNoRecovery=Windows recovery is off: there's no "Use a device".
UsbFound=Windows installation USB plugged in: %1
UsbNotFound=No Windows installation USB is plugged in. Plug it in before restarting.
UsbChoose=How do you want to restart?
UsbRecommended=%1 (recommended)
UsbOptionDevice=Restart into Advanced startup
UsbOptionFirmware=Restart into the BIOS/UEFI
UsbOptionPlain=Restart normally
UsbHintDevice=Then choose "Use a device" and your USB.
UsbHintFirmware=Then choose your USB in the boot menu (Boot).
UsbHintPlain=While the PC starts, press its boot menu key (F12, F11, F8 or Esc) and choose your USB.
MoreDetails=Show more details
LessDetails=Hide details
ExitTitle=Quit the installer?
ExitText=Nothing has been installed yet: you can open it again whenever you want.
ExitYes=Quit
ExitNo=Stay
UsbDetailDevice=Advanced startup (%1): Windows restarts into its blue options menu. Choose "Use a device" and then your USB. The BIOS/UEFI can be reached from that menu too.
UsbDetailFirmware=BIOS/UEFI (%1): restarts into the PC's settings. Look for the boot menu (Boot) and choose the USB, or put it first.
UsbDetailPlain=Normal restart (%1): in classic BIOS mode, Windows can't choose the boot device for you. While the PC starts, press its boot menu key; usually F12, F11, F8 or Esc.
UsbDetailSecureBoot=Secure Boot: only a signed USB starts. Make it with Microsoft's media creation tool, or with Rufus and the original Windows image.
UsbDetailNoRecovery=The Windows recovery environment (WinRE) is off, so Advanced startup wouldn't offer "Use a device"; that's why the BIOS/UEFI is suggested.
UsbRestartNote=The PC restarts in %1 seconds and Windows closes the programs that are open. To cancel it meanwhile, type shutdown /a in a console.
UsbRestartButton=Restart
UsbOptionNone=Don't restart now
UsbRestartFailedTitle=The restart couldn't be scheduled
UsbRestartFailedText=Windows rejected "%1": %2 (code %3). Try another option.
RestartLogNote=The log is open (and saved on your Desktop) in case you want to review it.
FinishedHeadingCancelled=Installation cancelled
FinishedHeadingWarnings=Finished, with warnings
FinishedHeadingBackup=Backup saved
FinishedHeadingOk=All done
LogSavedAt=Log saved on your Desktop:
NothingSelectedTitle=You haven't selected anything
NothingSelectedText=Select at least one app or option, or go back and choose a backup.

